**
# Allowlist, not blocklist: the context starts empty and only the paths a
# build actually reads are re-included. A blocklist kept missing new secret
# and artifact shapes (verified: deploy/selfhost/.env and packages/web/.next
# both entered image layers under the old list).
!package.json
!bun.lock
!tsconfig.json
!packages/
!packages/**
!scripts/
!scripts/fix-standalone-swc-helpers.ts
# The self-hosted compose builds from this same root context with
# deploy/selfhost/Dockerfile, which COPYs deploy/ — without these two lines
# that build has no deploy directory at all.
!deploy/
!deploy/**
#
# Everything below must stay AFTER every `!` negation, and must contain no
# further `!`: `!deploy/**` re-includes that whole directory, so only the
# exclusions after it take deploy/selfhost/.env and the auth.json render
# output back out, and Docker applies the LAST matching rule.
#
**/node_modules
**/.next*
**/dist
**/.wrangler
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.DS_Store
# Secrets at ANY depth. A bare `.env` only excludes the context root, so
# deploy/selfhost/.env (created by the quickstart) would still be COPYed into
# the pew-selfhost:local image — leaking real secrets into an image layer.
# `cp .env .env.bak` must not reopen the hole.
**/.env*
**/.dev.vars*
**/.rqlite-auth.json
**/.rqlite-auth.json.*
# The render script's staging file holds every plaintext password until the
# atomic rename; `.auth.json` alone does not match a `.tmp` suffix. Two
# spellings are needed, and not because of a leading dot (Docker's `*` DOES
# match one — verified): the default file is `.rqlite-auth.json`, whose name
# has a HYPHEN before `auth`, so `*.auth.json*` can never match it.
deploy/selfhost/*.auth.json
deploy/selfhost/*.auth.json.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
.git
# Agent/editor worktrees and scratch state at any depth: a root-anchored
# `.claude` only excludes the top-level directory (verified: a nested
# packages/web/.claude/worktrees copy entered the context).
**/.claude
**/.superpowers
# Playwright output: gitignored, but Docker does not read nested .gitignore
# files, so it would otherwise reach the image layers.
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
# Backup archives and their staging dirs (backup.sh output; the archive holds
# every password_hash/api_key, and build contexts are the repo root, so a
# build running while an archive exists would bake it into an image layer).
# The two patterns are not redundant: backup.sh's default name is
# backup-YYYY-MM-DD.db, but an operator may pass any path (`/var/backups/pew/
# pew.db`, `pre-cluster-*.db`, `dump.db`). A `*.db` inside the repo therefore
# must never reach a build context — verified: only the default name was being
# excluded while a `dump.db` next to it entered /ctx intact.
**/backup-*.db
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/.pew-backup.*/
logo.png
scripts/resize-logos.py
